WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
A 120 million Euro fine on X now has Washington asking to join the case. This is Omni View Europe, Episode 3. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. The Justice Department put that request before the European Union's General Court, Trading View Reports, in support of separate challenges already filed by X and by Elon Musk. They won a December 2025 decision by the European Commission's Set-aside. The Commission levied the penalty on the company

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.480
and on Musk together, for what it called breaches of the Digital Services Act.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.920
Seeking Alpha's dollar figure is 136.5 million.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.380
Assistant Attorney General Brett Schumate said Brussels had wrongly tried to stretch its

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:49.000
rules onto American firms that are neither present nor operating inside the block.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.040
The commission says the penalty followed two years of looking at the Blue Check System, the

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.100
ad archive, and researchers access to public data.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.800
It calls this the first non-compliance ruling under that law.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.700
Filing the papers does not wipe out the penalty.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.680
The general court still has to say whether Washington may sit in the case.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:12.720
Russian diplomats in Czechia face the strictest new paperwork across the region.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.000
From this week, they must warn Prague at least a day before they cross the border.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.520
Balkan Insight reports that the notice has to name the purpose, the exact route, how long

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.860
they will stay, and where.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:29.460
Foreign Minister Petra Machinka says Moscow already demands the same of Czech diplomats,

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:34.720
and that European governments are trying to stop intelligence officers traveling under a diplomatic

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:41.000
label. Since January, EU rules have required Russian diplomats to notify countries other than the

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:47.200
one that accredited them. States may go further. Martin Kukka, who leads the opposition ODS party,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.240
calls this only halfway. He says those diplomats can still arrive on Shengen visas,

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.260
and Prague cannot turn them away.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.440
Britain's early look at new American AI models

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.500
is the other shift.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.920
Insurance Business, citing Politico,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.400
