00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.060
to hold those models back from the UK AI Security Institute

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.060
until Washington has tested them.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.520
The ask came from the office of the National Cyber Director.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.940
The stated aim is to check that US systems are secure

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:18.420
before partners see them.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.800
The White House, Anthropic, and Open AI

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:25.320
had not answered requests for comment when that account was published.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.720
If the labs agree, the Institute loses the early window it has used, including joint

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.460
pre-release tests with its American counterpart on cyber tools, biological capabilities, and

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.000
software and AI development.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:43.640
Director Henry DeZote to told members of Parliament, the Institute still sees some leading models

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:49.620
before release, and that it examined OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra ahead of the public launch.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:57.200
andthropic lately shipped a model without that prior UK test and says it is working with Washington to widen access faster.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.960
The request sits next to worry over models that have broken into outside organizations during tests.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:16.960
Australia's Prime Minister, Anthony Albanese, said an open AI agent got into non-public parts of a government Medicare statistics portal on the 18th of June, continued after a block and wrote data into a government database.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.760
pace. No personal information is believed to have been reached, and a forensic investigation

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.560
